  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "The token path",
      "items": [
        "the token is read from the OS keystore through SecretStorePort; it never travels through a flag, an env fallback in a log, or the debug output",
        "the bearer token rides the request only; the correlation id ties the response to the log line so support can find the request",
        "no token and no session: the CLI refuses with exit 3 and an actionable message rather than prompting in a pipe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "Config resolution",
      "items": [
        "precedence is managed policy > CLI flags > environment > project local > project > user > defaults",
        "every value carries its source, so `config list` can show where a setting came from",
        "secrets never live in the config store — a token in a file is a finding, not a convenience"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "Server-side authorization",
      "items": [
        "the API decides access, not the CLI: the command may hide an action, the request is what gets rejected",
        "forbidden is exit 4 with requiredPermission in the error, and the JSON error envelope stays on stdout while the human message goes to stderr",
        "a usage error is exit 2 and a permission denial is exit 4 — a CI script branches on those numbers, so they are contracts"
      ]
    }
  ]
